      "rationale": "Categorizing incidents into system domains (hardware_device, software_application, database, network) is directly central to the query about hardware signals, giving a clean grouping axis. Sample values are sound readings of the short_description (software installation -> software_application; MySQL connection -> database)."
    },
    {
      "name": "software_keyword_present",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.45,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A bare boolean keyword flag is fairly generic and partly redundant with affected_system_domain; it offers limited independent leverage. However, as a complementary signal for isolating non-software (potentially hardware) incidents it retains some value. Values match the source text well."
    },
    {
      "name": "description_action_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.88,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Action-type categories (failure_malfunction, connectivity_issue, installation_request, etc.) provide a distinct behavioral axis that complements the domain column and can help distinguish hardware-typical failure/connectivity language. Sample values are well-grounded in the descriptions; NULL for unclear rows is acceptable."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.89,
  "rationale": "Two of the three columns (affected_system_domain, description_action_type) provide genuine, distinct grouping axes that directly serve the hardware-signal query, and all values are well-grounded in the short_description text with no observed hallucination. The software_keyword_present flag is more generic and partially redundant, lowering the holistic usefulness slightly but not the groundedness."
}

